==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|oure-selfe}}; equivalent to {{suffix|en|our|self}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/(ˌ)aʊə(ɹ)ˈsɛlf/|/(ˌ)ɑː(ɹ)ˈsɛlf/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-ourself.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛlf|s=2}}

===Pronoun===
{{en-pron|desc=first person|singular reflexive of|we}}

# {{lb|en|reflexive pronoun}} {{ng|The [[reflexive]] of the [[royal we|royal]] or [[editorial we]]}}: {{l|en|myself}} (as used by a monarch, writer or speaker who is referring to themself as {{m|en|we}}).
#: {{ux|en|In the present study, we will limit '''ourself''' to the simplest of cases.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1838|author=w:Charles Dickens|title=s:Sketches of Young Gentlemen
|passage=Without in any way committing '''ourself''' upon this point, we have merely to observe, that we are ready to receive sealed offers containing a full specification of age, temper, appearance, and condition{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1962|title=Princeton Alumni Weekly|volume=63|page=24
|passage=He then offered to guide us down to see for '''ourself''', but one look down that dark hole to the water about 60 feet below completely dampened our speluncean ardor.}}
# {{lb|en|reflexive pronoun}} {{ng|The reflexive of the [[generic]] [[we]]}}: {{l|en|oneself}}.
#: {{ux|en|We should love our neighbor as '''ourself'''.}}
# {{lb|en|colloquial}} {{non-gloss|Reflexive of "we" referring to an individual person being addressed, especially a person in the speaker's care.}}
#: {{ux|en|Hello Mrs Miggins. Did we manage to wash '''ourself''' this morning?}}
#: {{ux|en|Well done Timmy! Did we make that model '''ourself'''?|q = ''emphatic use''}}
# {{lb|en|AAVE}} {{ng|The reflexive of [[we]]}}: {{l|en|ourselves}}.

====Usage notes====
* The normal reflexive form of ''we'' is {{m|en|ourselves}}. This form can generally be used alternatively in the above cases, too.

====Coordinate terms====
* {{l|en|ourselves}} {{q|plural}}

